<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Philippe Guerrier</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1757–1845</span></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Philippe Guerrier (1757–1845) was a Haitian general who served as president from May 1844 until his death in April 1845. A veteran of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/haitian-revolution">Haitian Revolution</a> who had been made a duke under King <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/henri-christophe">Henri Christophe</a>, he was installed in old age by the mixed-race elite as the first of several elderly Black figurehead presidents, a practice later called the politique de doublure.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/philippe-guerrier.jpg" alt="Philippe Guerrier" width="211" height="300" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown authorUnknown author · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Philippe_Guerrier.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
